 Compatibility: deploy prebuilt Cloudflare Worker fetch handlers (ES modules, optionally bundled WASM) plus static assets. Static HTML and Vite/React/Vue/Svelte frontends work with a Worker serving env.ASSETS.fetch(request); Hono and other Workers-compatible fetch frameworks work server-side. Bundle dependencies locally. The backend does not build source or run npm, Node/Bun servers, containers, Python, native addons, persistent filesystems, or background daemons. nodejs_compat is limited compatibility, not a Node server. Next.js App Router and Pages Router use sites_prepare_next: it installs the supported OpenNext adapter, creates dedicated Freebuff configs while preserving user configs, builds the project and packages its Worker, public assets and private prerender cache. Use the returned manifestPath with sites_deploy. Sites automatically supplies an isolated framework R2 cache, durable revalidation queue and tag cache per environment; these are separate from the user database and file bucket. Do not upload a normal .next build or run OpenNext deploy/upload commands against a Cloudflare account. Other SSR frameworks still need a verified Workers adapter. Unsupported Next.js versions or Node/native-only libraries must be fixed before publishing; never bypass adapter version checks.
 
